<doxygen xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="compound.xsd" version="1.18.0" xml:lang="en-US">
  <compounddef id="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-c-api" kind="group">
    <compoundname>micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-c-api</compoundname>
    <title>C API</title>
    <briefdescription>
<para>There is no C API; C code is tested from C++. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>µTest++ is built on C++20 features, such as templates, concepts, and lambdas, which have no equivalent in C, so it has no C API.</para>
<para>To test C code, write the test cases in C++ and call the C functions from them. If the C headers do not declare their functions with <computeroutput>extern "C"</computeroutput> themselves, include them in an <computeroutput>extern "C"</computeroutput> block:</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="keyword">extern</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;C&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="preprocessor">#include<sp/>&quot;adder.h&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">ts.test<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Check<sp/>the<sp/>C<sp/>adder&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>[]<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal">&amp;<sp/>t)<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::eq<sp/>(add<sp/>(2,<sp/>3),<sp/>5));</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">});</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting>  </para>
    </detaileddescription>
  </compounddef>
</doxygen>
